Consider these official classification guidelines:

1. [025/94] 87.08 Bodies (including cabs) for trucks and/or pickup trucks
   Bodies for trucks or pickup trucks are the coachwork of those vehicles. Therefore, the classification of said bodies is under subheading 87.07.9090. Parts of such bodies are classified under subheading 87.08.2000, subject to the classification rules in the tariff. File 87.08 025/94
2. [011/92] 87.08 Classification of parts and accessories for vehicles made of hardened rubber
   87.08, 40.17, 40.16 - Classification of parts and accessories for vehicles made of hardened rubber. It is hereby clarified that goods made of hardened rubber (e.g., mudguards) are classified under heading 87.08 and not under heading 40.17, in view of Rule 2(a) to Section XVII and in light of the Explanatory Notes to the Brussels Nomenclature for heading 40.17, which exclude these goods from the scope of heading 40.17. In contrast to the above, parts and accessories for motor vehicles made of vulcanized rubber are classified under heading 40.16. File SHAM: 87.08 011/92
3. [014/18] Classification of Electric ATVs for Children
   Below is the decision made by the Supreme Classification Committee held on 7.11.17: The electric ATV shown in the picture, weighing approximately 65 kg, with a motor power of 1000 watts, a maximum (limited) speed of 8 km/h, a battery voltage of 48 volts, a seat height of approximately 65 cm, and a wheel diameter of 16 inches, shall be classified under subheading 87.03.8090, which refers to other motor vehicles principally designed for the transport of persons, powered by an electric motor. The classification shall not be determined under customs heading 95.03, which refers to wheeled toys, due to the lack of safety in use, lack of parental supervision, and the suitability of the ATV for an adult. Effective from 7.11.2017 014/18.

