=== WHAT TO RETURN ===
Return one or several HS codes so the item's correct full classification is sure to fall under one of them.

How many codes to give: if one code is clearly the only correct category the item belongs to, give just that one. If there are several options and you are not sure which code is right - either because you need more information about the item to decide, or because more than one code could reasonably apply - give all the options.

How deep to go: for each code, go down (chapter -> heading -> subheading) as far as you can while staying sure. Stop, and return the code at that level or list the different options, as soon as going deeper would depend on information you don't have, or on a classification choice you are not sure about.

When to stop at chapter / heading level VS when to split to several options:
- If one option is a subset of another in the list, return only the broader code.
- If several options together cover all headings in a chapter or all subheadings in a heading, return only the single higher-level code.
- Otherwise, list all distinct options.

=== HS LEVELS ===
- 2 digits: chapter (e.g., 84)
- 4 digits: heading (e.g., 8471)
- 6 digits: subheading (e.g., 847150)

