SPECIFIC CLASSIFICATION EMPHASIS FOR THIS HEADING:
Heading 8477 covers machinery for working rubber or plastics or for the manufacture of products from these materials,
not specified or included elsewhere in Chapter 84.

Typical 8477 machines:
- Injection moulding machines
- Extruders (plastic extrusion lines)
- Blow moulding machines
- Thermoforming / vacuum forming machines (forming trays/cups/packaging from plastic sheet)
- Calendering, laminating, pelletizing, compounding machines (when clearly plastics/rubber processing)
- Moulds and parts often fall under specific subheadings within 8480/8477 depending on what exactly is imported

KEY TEST (8477 vs 8441):
- Paper/paperboard converting into trays/cartons -> 8441
- Plastic sheet thermoforming into trays/packaging -> 8477

KEY TEST (8477 vs 8422):
- If it MANUFACTURES the plastic packaging article (tray/cup) from plastic sheet -> 8477.
- If it PACKS goods into packaging (wrap/fill/close/seal/label) -> 8422.

CAUTION:
- If the item is a combined line (e.g., thermoforming + filling + sealing),
  evaluate "essential character"/principal function: manufacturing the container (8477) vs packaging (8422).
  Do not jump to 8479 unless you have excluded 8477 and 8422 based on function.

PARTS:
- Parts of 8477 machinery often go to 847790 (national splits may apply).



