SPECIFIC CLASSIFICATION EMPHASIS FOR THIS HEADING:
Heading 8708 covers PARTS AND ACCESSORIES of motor vehicles of headings 8701-8705
(typically passenger cars, buses, trucks, etc.).

CRITICAL: 8708 is NOT a "default for anything used in a vehicle".
It is ONLY valid when ALL are true:
1) The item is a PART/ACCESSORY of a vehicle (not a complete machine of another heading)
2) It is suitable for use SOLELY or PRINCIPALLY with motor vehicles of 8701-8705
3) It is NOT excluded by "parts of general use" rules and NOT covered by a more specific heading

STEP 0 - FIRST QUESTION:
Is this a complete article with its OWN heading (by what it IS), even if used in a vehicle?
- If YES -> classify by that specific heading (NOT 8708)
- If NO -> proceed to 8708 analysis

STEP 1 - PARTS OF GENERAL USE (MUST CHECK):
Many generic items do NOT go to 8708 even if described "for a car/bus".
Examples of common "parts of general use" that stay in their own headings:
- Screws/bolts/nuts/washers -> 7318
- Springs -> 7320
- Plain bearings / ball bearings -> 8482
- Generic pipes/tubes/fittings (depending) -> Section XV headings

STEP 2 - "SOLELY OR PRINCIPALLY" TEST:
Evidence that supports 8708:
- Explicitly identified as vehicle-specific part (OEM part number for vehicle platform)
- Geometry/interface unique to vehicles
- Not reasonably usable outside vehicles
Evidence against 8708:
- Generic industrial component used across machines
- Standard electrical/electronic apparatus covered in Ch.85 (e.g., switches, sensors, connectors)
- Standard rubber/plastic articles not uniquely vehicle-specific

STEP 3 - EXAMPLES OF ITEMS THAT OFTEN BELONG IN 8708 (when vehicle-specific and not covered elsewhere):
- Body parts & accessories: bumpers, grills, panels, door trim
- Safety devices: seat belts, airbags (often in 8708 depending on national breakdown)
- Certain interior fittings: dashboards, consoles (if not covered elsewhere)
- Vehicle-specific mechanical parts not having a dedicated heading

STEP 4 - COMMON MISCLASSIFICATIONS TO AVOID:
Do NOT send to 8708 when the item is clearly classified elsewhere:
- Electrical switches/sensors (e.g., door safety edge sensor) -> 8536.xx (switches etc.)
- Electric motors -> 8501
- Pumps -> 8413
- Valves -> 8481
- Bearings -> 8482
- Rubber profiles/strips as simple rubber articles (if no electrical switching function) -> check 4016
- Textile webbing (as material) -> 5806/5903 etc. (NOT automatically 8708)

KEY RULE:
8708 is a "vehicle parts" heading of LAST RESORT after ruling out:
- (a) a more specific functional heading, and
- (b) parts of general use headings.


