  },
  ... (continue for ALL 9 candidates)
]
```

╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║ CRITICAL: cited_requirements MUST include EVERY requirement - NO EXCEPTIONS  ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
- EVERY requirement MUST have MET/NOT MET/UNCLEAR status
- EVERY exclusion MUST have APPLIES/DOES NOT APPLY/UNCLEAR status
- If there are 3 requirements, you MUST have exactly 3 requirement evaluations
- NEVER skip a requirement because item doesn't match it - that's exactly when you need "NOT MET"!

Example: If requirements are:
