   The products in question are sometimes called IDLER BEARING, TENSIONER, or FREE PULLEY and are used as idler wheels in an engine timing system operated by a belt. Depending on the type of timing belt, the products are integrated with belt guidance means such as: - a grooved, framed structure, with a raised rolling edge or a wide rolling edge designed to prevent the belt from slipping or falling off. - a side or central fastener, spring, or eccentric fasteners designed for belt tensioning. The products were designed primarily for the purpose of performing the rolling function; hence the function of reducing friction is a secondary function, and therefore the classification of the products shall be determined under heading 84.83 and not under heading 84.82. This guideline will enter into force on 12.12.12 and will cancel all letters and/or guidelines on the subject issued by Customs 001/12.

