SPECIFIC CLASSIFICATION EMPHASIS FOR THIS HEADING:
Heading 870880 = SUSPENSION SYSTEMS and parts thereof.
Think: "shock/strut/spring/arms/bushings that locate the wheel".

ESSENTIAL FEATURES (what 870880 IS):
- Complete suspension systems or their parts for vehicles 8701-8705
- Includes shock absorbers/struts/coilovers and many mechanical suspension members

STRONG INDICATORS FOR 870880:
- Keywords: suspension, shock absorber, strut, coilover, damper, spring (as part of strut/coilover),
  control arm, wishbone, trailing arm, stabilizer/anti-roll bar, sway bar link, bushing,
  ball joint (sometimes), suspension mount/top mount, knuckle-related suspension components
- Use/purpose: ride damping, wheel location, suspension adjustment, performance suspension kit

COMMON PITFALLS (parts-of-general-use & other headings):
- Springs alone can be "parts of general use" -> 7320 (if imported as standalone springs, not as part of strut/coilover assembly)
- Rubber bushes/grommets as generic rubber articles -> 4016 (if not clearly vehicle-suspension-specific or if treated as general rubber articles in your tariff logic)
- Bearings in suspension/hub context -> 8482 when imported as bearings
- Fasteners/bolts/nuts used in suspension -> 7318
- Steering parts (tie rods, steering gear parts) -> 870894/870899 depending on national tree

CORE RULE: COILOVERS & SHOCKS
- "Coilover" (shock + spring/adjuster assembly) is a classic 870880 item.
- "Shock piston" as an internal component:
  * If clearly a part of shock absorber/suspension and vehicle-specific -> still 870880 in most practical trees.

QUESTIONS THAT RESOLVE 870880 (minimal):
- Is the item intended to DAMP/LOCATE the wheel (shock/strut/arm/bushing)?
- Is it a complete coilover/strut assembly or a shock absorber component?
- If only a generic spring or generic rubber part -> consider 7320 / 4016 before 8708.

QUICK EXAMPLES:
- "shock piston coilovers" -> 870880
- "rear suspension arm hinge insert" (if a bushing/insert in suspension arm) -> usually 870880, unless it is clearly a generic bushing/article (4016) by your rules
- "control arm" -> 870880


